00:01:10.973 --> 00:01:14.020
I think that we are in
a very similar place

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:17.510
to where we were in
internet stocks in 2000.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.110
I think when you have

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:23.240
these massive transformation
technology shifts,

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:26.740
there's a moment where
everybody gets excited about it.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:28.650
And, you know, for me

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:33.080
the internet was happening
in '95, six, seven

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:35.660
but you started to really
see the stock market

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:38.180
embrace with those IPO's in '98, '99.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:41.920
And then obviously in
April, March, April, 2000

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:44.150
you had the, the collapsing of it

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:45.030
at the time

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:46.733
of the stocks

00:01:46.733 --> 00:01:48.040
at the time, a lot of people talked

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.770
about the internet being a fad

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.370
and it never been meaningful

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:53.006
for businesses, blah, blah, blah.

00:01:53.006 --> 00:01:55.470
What happened in reality was the internet

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.770
was this game changing
revolution of technology

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:00.135
but a lot of the early projects

00:02:00.135 --> 00:02:03.230
were just overpriced on the excitement.

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:06.390
I think we're absolutely
in the replication of this.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:08.890
I think NFTs are going to be

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:10.590
a framework that we trade in,

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:14.620
collect in, utility in, access in,

