but I think some of the projects

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:19.770
that we're seeing right now

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:22.272
on the individual pieces

00:02:22.272 --> 00:02:24.463
are going to burst.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.780
- So you have a long
experience in marketing

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:32.540
and are obviously quite skilled at that.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:35.570
Until recently, Bitcoin
was widely considered

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:36.620
to have a marketing problem.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.480
Like people just didn't
get it, like people,

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:39.600
the mainstream just didn't get it.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.690
Now that's changed a little bit

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:41.870
just because of the price.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:42.870
But if you were,

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:43.790
if you had to give kind of

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.470
like the elevator pitch for Bitcoin

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:46.944
like the quick marketing soundbite,

00:02:46.944 --> 00:02:48.040
what would you say?

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.853
Like, how would you sell
Bitcoin to the masses?

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:55.380
- You know, if I was selling Bitcoin

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.380
I would, I would speak about history.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:00.130
You know, why did gold do XYZ?

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:01.436
Why did Fiat happen?

00:03:01.436 --> 00:03:06.050
Like, what is the human
psychology to acceptance?

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:09.380
I would speak about
things that could happen.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:12.400
Like what if Amazon accepts it?

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.950
What if XYZ country invests

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.380
aggressively at it?

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.690
So I think there's a lot of logical steps

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:21.290
to continue the

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:23.430
affirmation

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.250
and confirmation of the currency,

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:27.660
and I think history has proven that,

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:31.370
and I would use history and examples

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.053
of one domino effect

00:03:33.053 --> 00:03:35.623
that could change the outcome

00:03:35.623 --> 00:03:37.963
for the people that are cynical about it.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.740
- So just to follow up
on that, how would you

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.130
how would you market NFTs?

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:43.320
You know, and NFTs,

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.470
like right now, there's all these people

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:45.947
being like why is someone spending

00:03:45.947 --> 00:03:47.630
$70 million on a JPEG?

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:49.010
If you just had to quickly explain

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:51.220
to somebody what the value is of an NFT,

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:52.170
what would you say?

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:54.320
- I usually go down the route of

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:56.630
do you know somebody who's
bought a Fortnight skin

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:57.913
for a hundred bucks,

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.740
do you think a blue check

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.973
on Instagram is worth something,

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.260
I educate them for a minute

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:06.930
on the metadata on the NFTs

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.410
and speak about access, membership clubs,

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:11.585
VIP, treatments, one-on-one dinners,

00:04:11.585 --> 00:04:13.830
and talk about all the charity events

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:16.330
and things that are sold
when people get access

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:18.330
to things that they can't get access to.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.943
- So getting back to the topic,

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.170
keeping on this whole idea

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:24.743
of the NFT bubble, et cetera,

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.710
nonetheless

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:28.790
NFTs,

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:30.408
how would you translate that

00:04:30.408 --> 00:04:32.280
into the real world?

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.760
How would you translate,

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:34.900
You know, you've been in the business

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.994
of selling physical goods.

00:04:36.994 --> 00:04:39.930
So how would you translate

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.260
the NFT from intellectual property

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.370
into the physical world?

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.798
How, how will, how will that come about?

00:04:46.798 --> 00:04:49.090
- I think people really
under underestimating

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:51.200
and undereducated on the smart contracts,

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.070
and

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:53.100
the reality is

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.280
you could sell the digital asset

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:57.490
then deliver the individual,

00:04:57.490 --> 00:04:58.860
the physical good

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.040
but then in the smart contract,

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:00.970
let me give an example.

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:03.210
If I decide I have a book
coming out in November

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:04.380
but then I'm a free agent

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:05.810
and I was going to sign another book deal.

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.040
Now I'm debating,

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.060
Should I just NFT my book after that

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:12.020
print 200,000 copies

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:15.050
make an NFT replication of the cover,

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:18.840
make 190,000 that look
exactly like the cover.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:21.300
And if you buy it for 20 bucks, the NFT,

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.450
I send you the book it's
literally, and you have now

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:24.794
this little digital asset

00:05:24.794 --> 00:05:26.190
that you might be able to trade

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:27.450
on to make some of your dollars back,

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:28.283
or what have you.

00:05:28.283 --> 00:05:30.350
But the nurse 10,000 covers left.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.790
9,000 of those can be silver covers

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.160
and they may be a hundred dollars,

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.552
but what that does in the smart contract

00:05:35.552 --> 00:05:38.160
is it allows you to be
part of my book club,

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.980
and once a month, once a week,

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:41.569
whatever I decide in the smart contract,

00:05:41.569 --> 00:05:43.450
I will go with that small group

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:44.780
and do Q and A learnings

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.920
that leaves a hundred gold books

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.900
that might be things
like one on one dinners

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:50.080
or live conference,

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:51.780
and maybe one platinum book

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:52.613
that is somebody

00:05:52.613 --> 00:05:53.870
that gets to spend a month with me.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:57.800
The access underneath the smart contract,

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.010
I think is going to end up being

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:01.840
the aha for a lot of people

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.030
as they become more educated,

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:04.770
that it's not just a JPEG.

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:05.603
Not to mention,

00:06:05.603 --> 00:06:07.840
people care about the
ownership of provenance.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.860
And as that becomes social currency

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:11.720
and the way we live,

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.390
it's no different than in 1999

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:14.223
when I told my friends

00:06:14.223 --> 00:06:15.462
that everybody would online date

00:06:15.462 --> 00:06:17.500
and they laughed me out of the room.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.830
They were unable to see the chess moves

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:21.980
to how society would evolve.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.150
I believe in 15 years,

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:23.983
people are going to look at

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:25.470
people's public wallets

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:27.170
to see what they have bought

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:29.030
to become a conversation piece

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:31.750
or a social currency layer

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:33.670
the way that logos are,

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:36.110
the way that followers
on social media are,

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:37.530
the way that your Wikipedia

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.783
or Google search results are.

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:41.710
- That's funny you say that,

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:44.230
cause I'm about to do
that right now with you.

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:47.300
Gary, you tweeted in 2013

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.810
that you just bought, using Bitcoin,

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:51.010
Google smart pants

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:53.800
and had it delivered by
a drone in 21 minutes.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:57.500
First of all, must be a
very expensive pair of pants

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.150
in today's dollar terms in seconds.

00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:02.180
You know, you know,
what was your experience

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:05.160
with paying something with Bitcoin,

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:07.140
should it be used as a currency?

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:09.183
What, what, what are
your thoughts on that?

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.380
- Should be, I apologize

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:14.329
should be my experience was in 2013.

00:07:14.329 --> 00:07:15.162
Go ahead

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:19.453
- Yeah, should Bitcoin
be used as a currency?

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:23.660
- It is, it's not even a should.

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:24.720
This is not about predictions.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:27.160
People accept Bitcoin all the time.

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.580
It's it's already happened.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:32.120
The question becomes what happens next.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:33.350
I think this, you know

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:35.690
Bitcoin is so much further along

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:37.330
than the majority of things

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:40.810
that have come before it
as an exceptive currency.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:41.950
To me,

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:43.010
I don't get

00:07:43.010 --> 00:07:43.843
to say

00:07:43.843 --> 00:07:45.410
more to most humans get to say

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:47.540
what should or shouldn't be accepted.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:50.190
If enough people believe in it,

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.040
then it becomes, you know,

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.590
I always remind people,

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:56.620
somebody used to live in the world

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.480
before gold meant anything.

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:02.380
You know, we didn't
have great documentation

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:05.640
but gold was a created ecosystem.

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:07.150
Should gold be accepted?

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:08.030
- What should be the currency

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:10.693
of the world is my question to you.

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:13.450
- Whatever enough of the people

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.380
in the world accept, right.

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:17.590
Humans create their ecosystems.

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:18.423
I don't think,

00:08:18.423 --> 00:08:20.110
I don't think it's the game of should.

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:22.550
This is a game of how
has it always happened?

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:25.200
People used to trade berries for sheep.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:29.329
People used to trade furs for, for people.

00:08:29.329 --> 00:08:31.960
People used to trade high-end wine

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:33.840
for workers to build things.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:36.730
I mean, I laugh at people's naivete

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:39.220
to think what is going on today,

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:40.800
or what we grew up with

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:43.000
is the end all be all.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.830
That's just laughable.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.440
Human race will continue to evolve,

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:48.920
and if anything,

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:51.020
I think it makes more sense

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:54.120
that things, that are
digital become the currency

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:56.030
as we go that route there's a race.

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:57.400
- Do you see Bitcoin

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:59.020
becoming the currency of the world

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:01.080
that everyone will start using, and...

00:09:02.546 --> 00:09:05.190
- (sighs) You know, I'd like to

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:06.517
answer things that I understand

00:09:06.517 --> 00:09:07.700
and you can see the conviction

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:09.140
I come in on the other questions.

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:09.973
I really don't know.

00:09:09.973 --> 00:09:10.806
You know, for me,

00:09:10.806 --> 00:09:13.770
the reason I've gone harder into NFT

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:15.530
than let's say currencies

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.520
is 'cause I just enjoy it more.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.020
You know, I wasn't the kind

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:20.250
of person that really

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.700
traded equities my whole life.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:25.300
I haven't spent the meaningful hours

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:26.840
that I think other people have

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:29.810
around really being able
to answer that question.

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:31.740
What I can tell you is,

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:33.360
people are naive,

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:34.790
And if they don't understand

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:36.910
that a shocking number of people

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:38.530
have accepted this,

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:40.330
I think there's a lot of conversation

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:42.520
of what happens to the dollar

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:45.630
when it goes off of the gold
standards in the seventies.

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:47.700
I think there's a lot going on

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:49.530
with our society

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:51.510
and our relationships with governments.

00:09:51.510 --> 00:09:56.510
And I think the ingredients
are in place for Bitcoin end.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:09:57.973
You know, you've got to understand

00:09:57.973 --> 00:09:59.820
that if Bitcoin hits

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:03.490
and becomes a currency of society,

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:05.810
well that leads to a
lot of other currencies,

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.100
and a lot of other variables

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:09.580
like NFTs to also follow suit.

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:12.873
And it creates a real
digital finance economy.

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:15.870
- So for a long time

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:17.710
people have been getting really frustrated

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:19.260
with our current social media platforms,

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:20.630
in particular Facebook, right.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:21.780
In terms of, you know,

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:24.240
keeping our data, selling
our data, you know,

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:26.640
individuals having limited control

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:28.860
over these sort of centralized platforms.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:31.640
And, but we still haven't
really seen anything

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:33.340
truly disrupt the current model

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:35.190
the sort of Facebook Twitter model.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:36.330
I guess my question is

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:38.580
how do you see the future of social media?

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:39.950
Do you think blockchain technology

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:40.950
will play a part of it?

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.620
Do you see a decentralized social media

